  "title": "University of San Carlos: Downtown Campus - Bernard Bonk Library",
  "text": "University of San Carlos: Downtown Campus - Bernard Bonk Library Home About Us Message from the Director Organizational Structure Rules of Use Contact Us Our Services Acquisitions List Book Blogs Creative Bibliotherapy Information Literacy Program AV Centers Services SHS Research Paper Collection Pathfinder/Indexes Services for Faculty Library Services Tutorials Linkages Electronic Resources Caroliniana Collections Cebuano Studies Center Free/Open Access Database Free/Open Access eBooks Intranet Access Database OAR / OER Directory Online Subscription Scholarly Journals SVD Network Database Webliography Web Logs/Blogs FAQs USC USC Home ISMIS JavaScript must be enabled on your browser for this PAC to work properly. Library Advisory Downtown Campus American Corner Cebu Bonk Library Law and Governance Library Library Staff Talamban Campus Josef Baumgartner Learning Resource Center Cebuano Studies Center American Corner Cebu Filipiniana Humanities Sci-Tech Social Science Library Staff OPAC Downtown Campus - Bernard Bonk Library Bernard Bonk Library ❮ ❯ The Bernard Bonk Library is a subject discipline library situated at the 2nd floor of the Arthur Dingman building in Downtown Campus with a 239 seating capacity, catering the School of Business and Economics which is composed of following departments: Accountancy, Business Administration, Economics and Hospitality and Tourism. It offers resources and services focused on business, economics, finance, hospitality and tourism and other related fields. Typically upkeep academic, research, entrepreneurship and professional development for students, faculty members, researchers, administration and industry professionals. Programs and Services Circulation Counter Check-out, checked-in, renewal and reservation/request. Reference & information Queries (onsite and online) Knowledge Navigation Center Use of computer terminals with a fee. Printing and Photocopying Printing and Photocopying service at the circulation section. Database searching assistance Provides instruction and assistance on how to access subscribed online databases and Online Public Access Catalog (OPAC). Information Literacy Program Level 1, 2, 3 and 4. Current awareness Eboard and new acquisitions display. Library Hours Mondays to Saturdays 7:30AM - 5:30PM Contact Information Jacquelyn A. Gabat, RL SBE Librarian for BA, HT & Graduate Programs E-mail Address: jagabat@usc.edu.ph Tel No: 401-2300 local 570 Rave Ann E. Javier SBE Librarian for Accountancy and Economics E-mail Address: rejavier@usc.edu.ph Tel No: 401-2300 local 570 Bernard Bonk Library Help Desk E-mail Address: blcirc@usc.edu.ph Tel No: 401-2300 local 570 Return to top of page",
